// trap: a true rule that is not inductive alone, and that no mined lemma helps.
// The light turns off only while no door is ajar or open; a door cracks open only while no
// light is off; Swing opens an ajar door with no guard. So no state has a light off and a
// door open, at any bound. The rule is not inductive alone: from the unreachable state
// (light off, door ajar), Swing breaks it, and no mined lemma rules that state out, since
// the light and the door are not related by a key. The prover generalizes that CTI into
// "no light is off while a door is ajar", which is inductive, and proves the rule with it
// (#428); BFS finds nothing. z3_lemma.rdra writes the same fact as a `.lemma()`.
// expect MultiForbidden_Light_0: native=ok tlc=ok z3=proved bfs=ok,ok,ok
// TLC's StateModel_ runs (#201) report both deadlocks: no step repeats, so no cycle hides
// them (every light off with every door closed, and the other way round).
// expect Deadlock_Door_state_closed: native=counterexample tlc=counterexample
// expect Deadlock_Light_state_on: native=counterexample tlc=counterexample
entity Light "照明" { id: Int @pk  state: Enum(on, off) @default(on) }
entity Door "扉" { id: Int @pk  state: Enum(closed, ajar, open) @default(closed) }
usecase Install "照明設置"
usecase Fit "扉設置"
usecase TurnOff "消灯"
usecase Crack "少し開ける"
usecase Swing "開ける"
creates(Install, Light)
creates(Fit, Door)
transitions(TurnOff, Light.state, on -> off)
transitions(Crack, Door.state, closed -> ajar)
transitions(Swing, Door.state, ajar -> open)
condition DoorsShut "開いた扉がない"
holds(DoorsShut, Light.state == on).none(Door.state in (ajar, open))
applies_to(DoorsShut, TurnOff)
condition LightsOn "消えた照明がない"
holds(LightsOn, Door.state == closed).none(Light.state == off)
applies_to(LightsOn, Crack)
forbidden(Light, Door, Light.state == off, Door.state == open).global()
